[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Document" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/core/document.gd" id="1_doc"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_doc")
id = &"d17_chart_trace"
title = "C-4 trace — Run 9, day 31"
byline = "still on the drum; the paper ran out, the pens did not"
hand = 0
body = "RECORDER C-4. SIX PEN. 12 IN.
RUN 9 / CHAMBER B / DAY 31
04 JUNE 1977

PEN 1  TEMP        steady, 36.4 - 36.7
PEN 2  ACTIVITY    steady, low
PEN 3  RESP        steady, 12 - 14
PEN 4  LUMINAIRE   on at 0600, off at 0800
PEN 5  DOOR        closed
PEN 6  OBSERVER    at station 0555 - 0805

The six lines run the width of the sheet in
the same shapes they have run for thirty
days. Nothing on this page is remarkable.

At the right hand edge, where the paper ends,
pen 4 and pen 6 continue onto the drum itself
for about two inches, in pencil-thin ink,
and stop together.

Pens 1, 2 and 3 do not continue onto the
drum. They stop at the paper's edge.

Somebody has written along the drum, small,
following the ink:

     PAPER OUT 0806. RE-ORDER.
     STAYED FOR THE WINDOW."
